# Build output of the C# gameplay module.
#
# Local rather than a line in the repo root .gitignore: that file is shared by
# eleven worktrees on this machine, and a line added there to solve a problem
# in one example project is a line somebody else's next commit can carry.
#
# The native build dir and resources/_cooked are already covered by the root
# .gitignore; these two are not, because MSBuild puts its output inside the
# project rather than under build/.
csharp/bin/
csharp/obj/

# Captured evidence, regenerable and therefore NOT tracked.
#
# A screenshot committed next to the code it depicts goes stale silently:
# nothing fails when the game changes and the picture does not, and the next
# reader takes an image of a build that no longer exists as a description of
# the current one.  AGENTS.md says how to regenerate them instead.
shots/
